@startuml deep_review_architecture

title Deep Code Review - OpenCode MVP Architecture

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

actor Developer

package "OpenCode" {
  component "<b>/deep-review</b> command\n(custom prompt entry)" as Command <<custom>>
  component "<b>/send-comments</b> command\n(explicit numbered selection)" as SendComments <<custom>>
  component "Send-comments agent\n(custom primary, least privilege)\nfinding selection and tool invocation" as SendAgent <<custom>>

  component "Plan agent\n(built-in primary)\norchestration, result verification,\ndeduplication and final report formatting" as Plan <<built-in>>

  component "<b>bitbucket MCP tools</b>\n(externally configured)\nPR metadata, comments\nand comment creation" as BitbucketMcp <<external>>

  package "Jira MCP (externally configured)" {
    component "<b>get_issue</b>\nread issue summary, description,\nstatus and type" as JiraIssueMcp <<external>>
    component "<b>get_issue_comments</b>\nread one comment page\nwith cursor and limit" as JiraCommentsMcp <<external>>
  }

  artifact "Requirement context\nuntrusted Jira data, provenance,\ncompleteness status and warnings" as RequirementContext

  component "<b>deep-code-review</b> skill\n(custom SKILL.md)\nworkflow, review contracts\nand progressive disclosure" as Skill <<custom>>

  artifact "Shared review input\nrequirement context, target diff,\nbase/head, repository guidance\nand review scope" as ReviewInput

  package "Three fresh focused review tasks" {
    together {
      component "1. Solution and architecture\nfresh Explore invocation\nrequirements, completeness, design,\ninterfaces and cross-domain impact" as ArchitectureReview <<built-in>>
      component "2. Unit correctness\nfresh Explore invocation\nimplementation bugs, edge cases,\ntests and regressions" as UnitReview <<built-in>>
      component "3. Code polish\nfresh Explore invocation\nclarity, conventions, naming,\nstyle and small issues" as PolishReview <<built-in>>
    }
  }

  component "OpenCode repository tools\nread, grep, glob, read-only Git,\napproved project checks\nand optional experimental LSP" as RepositoryTools <<built-in>>

  artifact "Repository context\ndiff, AGENTS.md, source code,\ntests and check results" as Repository

  artifact "Three independent layer results\ncoverage, findings, evidence,\nchecks and limitations" as LayerResults

  artifact "Complete text review report\nall three layers, shown in OpenCode" as Report
}

database "Customer Jira Data Center" as Jira
database "Customer Bitbucket Data Center" as Bitbucket

Developer -right-> Command
Command -down-> Plan : PR URL + requirement

Plan -left-> JiraIssueMcp : one call\nvalidated issue key or URL
Plan -left-> JiraCommentsMcp : cursor 0, limit 100\nuntil next_cursor is null
JiraIssueMcp -down-> Jira : read-only MCP request
JiraCommentsMcp -down-> Jira : read-only MCP request
JiraIssueMcp -down-> RequirementContext : issue fields
JiraCommentsMcp -down-> RequirementContext : validated comment pages
RequirementContext -down-> ReviewInput
Plan -right-> BitbucketMcp : validate explicit PR URL\nand immutable revisions

Plan -down-> Skill : load protocol
Skill ..> ArchitectureReview : layer 1 rubric + LayerResult schema
Skill ..> UnitReview : layer 2 rubric + LayerResult schema
Skill ..> PolishReview : layer 3 rubric + LayerResult schema
Skill ..> Report : exact Markdown format

Plan ..> RepositoryTools : establish target and run checks
RepositoryTools -down-> Repository
Repository -down-> ReviewInput
Plan -down-> ReviewInput : assemble one scope snapshot

Plan -down-> ArchitectureReview : invoke with shared input
Plan -down-> UnitReview : invoke with shared input
Plan -down-> PolishReview : invoke with shared input
ReviewInput ..> ArchitectureReview : same input, no prior findings
ReviewInput ..> UnitReview : same input, no prior findings
ReviewInput ..> PolishReview : same input, no prior findings

ArchitectureReview ..> RepositoryTools : focused inspection
UnitReview ..> RepositoryTools : focused inspection
PolishReview ..> RepositoryTools : focused inspection

ArchitectureReview -down-> LayerResults : layer 1 result
UnitReview -down-> LayerResults : layer 2 result
PolishReview -down-> LayerResults : layer 3 result
LayerResults -up-> Plan : all layers completed

Plan -right-> Report : verified and deduplicated findings\nstrict model-rendered Markdown
Report -left-> Developer
Developer -down-> SendComments : /send-comments 1, 3\nafter report validation or discussion
Report ..> SendComments : review target and numbered findings
Plan ..> SendComments : later numbered findings\nfrom review checks and discussion
SendComments -down-> SendAgent : explicit selected numbers
SendAgent -down-> BitbucketMcp : verify PR, read comments,\ncreate selected comments sequentially
BitbucketMcp -down-> Bitbucket : exact start-line anchor: inline\notherwise: general PR comment
SendAgent -up-> Developer : placement reason + status\nconfirmed comment IDs

note right of Plan
  Configure the built-in Plan agent for this workflow:
  deny edits and review-posting integrations;
  allow only explicitly approved read-only Git commands
  and project checks; allow only Explore through task;
  allow only get_issue and get_issue_comments
  for Jira, plus Bitbucket PR read.
end note

note bottom of Skill
  Keep one concise orchestration skill.
  Store each detailed layer rubric, the LayerResult
  contract, report contract and exact report format
  as direct references.
end note

note bottom of ReviewInput
  Freeze the review target before starting the layers.
  Every layer receives the same requirement and diff scope.
  Do not pass findings between layers.
end note

note bottom of LayerResults
  Dispatch and run all three layers in parallel, with overlapping
  child-session execution, even when one finds issues. Stop with a
  parallel-run failure if overlap cannot be confirmed; never fall back.
  Preserve each finding's layer and evidence. The Plan agent
  verifies and deduplicates only after all results are available.
end note

note right of JiraCommentsMcp
  The MCP server is configured outside this project.
  Call get_issue exactly once. Page comments from cursor 0
  with limit 100 until next_cursor is null.
  Validate page shape, cursor progress and tool output.
  Map issue_type to issueType, author objects to the
  existing author string, and created_at/updated_at to
  created/updated. Preserve trust, provenance, comments
  and completeness metadata. Keep Jira text untrusted.
  On errors or truncation, preserve fetched data, mark
  requirement context incomplete and add a sanitized warning.
  Do not use Jira REST, shell, generic HTTP or a fallback tool.
end note

note bottom of Report
  Number verified findings consecutively.
  /deep-review remains read-only; only /send-comments
  can request publication of explicit numbers.
end note

note right of BitbucketMcp
  The MCP server is configured outside this project.
  Parse an explicit PR URL; never search for a target.
  Revalidate the open state and reviewed head before writes.
  Check exact duplicates through paginated PR comments.
  Render severity-only comment headings without finding numbers.
  Remove Location only from inline comments.
  Try each location's stated start line in report order.
  Use an unverified general fallback when no anchor succeeds.
  Post sequentially and return confirmed comment IDs.
  Stop before publication on stale-head or read failures.
  Continue with the next finding after a write failure.
  Phase 2 PR-context augmentation is not included.
end note

@enduml
